# Byte-stable checkout policy.
#
# RapidForensic validates evidence and fixtures by SHA-256. Any automatic
# newline conversion would make committed hashes differ per platform
# (known-answer QC broke on Windows checkouts with core.autocrlf=true).
# `-text` preserves every file's bytes exactly, on every platform.
* -text

# Windows shell scripts stay text with CRLF in the working tree.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
